    },
    "excluded_steps": [],
    "format_errors": [],
    "steps": [
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 132,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 133,
        "char_start": 0,
        "effective_step": 1,
        "end_token_index": 49,
        "near_end": false,
        "prefix_token_count": 50,
        "step_number": 1,
        "text": "Step 1: Let \\( c \\) be a root of the quadratic equation \\( x^2 + ax + b = 0 \\). Then, by definition, we have:\n\\[ c^2 + ac + b = 0. \\]"
      },
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 401,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 402,
        "char_start": 135,
        "effective_step": 2,
        "end_token_index": 177,
        "near_end": false,
        "prefix_token_count": 178,
        "step_number": 2,
        "text": "Step 2: Since \\( c^2 - 2 \\) is also a root, it must satisfy the same quadratic equation:\n\\[ (c^2 - 2)^2 + a(c^2 - 2) + b = 0. \\]\nExpanding this, we get:\n\\[ c^4 - 4c^2 + 4 + ac^2 - 2a + b = 0. \\]\nRearranging terms, we obtain:\n\\[ c^4 + (a - 4)c^2 + (4 - 2a + b) = 0. \\]"
      },
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 508,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 509,
        "char_start": 404,
        "effective_step": 3,
        "end_token_index": 232,
        "near_end": false,
        "prefix_token_count": 233,
        "step_number": 3,
        "text": "Step 3: We now have two equations:\n1. \\( c^2 + ac + b = 0 \\)\n2. \\( c^4 + (a - 4)c^2 + (4 - 2a + b) = 0 \\)"
      },
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 612,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 613,
        "char_start": 511,
        "effective_step": 4,
        "end_token_index": 270,
        "near_end": false,
        "prefix_token_count": 271,
        "step_number": 4,
        "text": "Step 4: From the first equation, express \\( b \\) in terms of \\( c \\) and \\( a \\):\n\\[ b = -c^2 - ac. \\]"
      },
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 841,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 842,
        "char_start": 615,
        "effective_step": 5,
        "end_token_index": 389,
        "near_end": false,
        "prefix_token_count": 390,
        "step_number": 5,
        "text": "Step 5: Substitute \\( b = -c^2 - ac \\) into the second equation:\n\\[ c^4 + (a - 4)c^2 + (4 - 2a - c^2 - ac) = 0. \\]\nSimplify the equation:\n\\[ c^4 + (a - 4)c^2 + 4 - 2a - c^2 - ac = 0, \\]\n\\[ c^4 + (a - 5)c^2 - ac + 4 - 2a = 0. \\]"
      },
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 1312,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 1314,
        "char_start": 844,
        "effective_step": 6,
        "end_token_index": 537,
        "near_end": false,
        "prefix_token_count": 538,
        "step_number": 6,
        "text": "Step 6: For the above equation to hold for all roots \\( c \\), the coefficients of corresponding powers of \\( c \\) must be zero. Therefore, we set up the system of equations:\n1. The coefficient of \\( c^4 \\): \\( 1 = 0 \\) (which is always true and does not provide new information).\n2. The coefficient of \\( c^3 \\): \\( -a = 0 \\Rightarrow a = 0 \\).\n3. The coefficient of \\( c^2 \\): \\( a - 5 = 0 \\Rightarrow a = 5 \\).\n4. The constant term: \\( 4 - 2a = 0 \\Rightarrow a = 2 \\)."
      },
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 1579,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 1580,
        "char_start": 1316,
        "effective_step": 7,
        "end_token_index": 590,
        "near_end": false,
        "prefix_token_count": 591,
        "step_number": 7,
        "text": "Step 7: We see that there is no consistent value of \\( a \\) that satisfies all these conditions simultaneously. This implies that the only possible values for \\( a \\) are those that make the polynomial structure consistent, which leads us to check specific values."
      },
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 1797,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 1799,
        "char_start": 1582,
        "effective_step": 8,
        "end_token_index": 691,
        "near_end": false,
        "prefix_token_count": 692,
        "step_number": 8,
        "text": "Step 8: If \\( a = 0 \\), then from \\( b = -c^2 \\), substituting back, we get:\n\\[ c^2 - 2 \\text{ is also a root, so } (c^2 - 2)^2 = c^4 - 4c^2 + 4 = 0. \\]\nThis simplifies to \\( c^2 = 2 \\), giving \\( c = \\pm \\sqrt{2} \\)."
      },
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 2027,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 2029,
        "char_start": 1801,
        "effective_step": 9,
        "end_token_index": 797,
        "near_end": false,
        "prefix_token_count": 798,
        "step_number": 9,
        "text": "Step 9: If \\( a = 5 \\), then from \\( b = -c^2 - 5c \\), substituting back, we get:\n\\[ (c^2 - 2)^2 + 5(c^2 - 2) + (-c^2 - 5c) = 0. \\]\nThis simplifies to \\( c^4 + c^2 - 10c - 6 = 0 \\), which does not generally hold for all \\( c \\)."
      },
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 2254,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 2256,
        "char_start": 2031,
        "effective_step": 10,
        "end_token_index": 902,
        "near_end": true,
        "prefix_token_count": 903,
        "step_number": 10,
        "text": "Step 10: If \\( a = 2 \\), then from \\( b = -c^2 - 2c \\), substituting back, we get:\n\\[ (c^2 - 2)^2 + 2(c^2 - 2) + (-c^2 - 2c) = 0. \\]\nThis simplifies to \\( c^4 - 2c^2 - 2c = 0 \\), which does not generally hold for all \\( c \\)."
      }
